                                        <h1 class="MarginTopTwoElement TextSizeThreeXL BoldFontElement TightTrackingElement GrayNineHundredTextElement SmallTextSizeFourXL">Privacy Policy</h1>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Stone and Story Privacy Policy</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Stone and Story (“we”, “us” or “our”) respects your privacy. This policy explains how we collect, use, store and protect personal information when you visit our website, contact us or use our interior design services. We process personal information in accordance with applicable UK data protection law, including the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Information we may collect</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">
                                                Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect your name, email address, telephone number, postal address, project details, property information, preferences and any other information you choose to provide. If you contact us, we may keep a record of your correspondence. We may also collect technical information about your use of our website, such as your IP address, browser type and pages visited, including through cookies or similar
                                                technologies.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">How we use your information</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">
                                                We may use personal information to respond to enquiries, discuss and deliver interior design services, prepare proposals or quotations, manage projects, communicate with you, process payments where applicable, maintain our records, improve our website and services, and meet legal or regulatory obligations. We will send marketing communications only where permitted by law. You can opt out of marketing at any time by using the unsubscribe option or
                                                contacting us.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Our lawful bases for processing</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">We process personal information where it is necessary to take steps at your request before entering into a contract, perform a contract with you, comply with a legal obligation, pursue our legitimate interests (such as responding to enquiries, managing our business and improving our services), or where you have given consent. Where we rely on consent, you may withdraw it at any time.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Sharing your information</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">
                                                We may share information with service providers who support our business, such as website hosting, IT, communications, payment or professional service providers. They may process information only as needed to provide their services to us and are expected to protect it. We may also disclose information where required by law or where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims. We do not sell your personal information.
                                        </p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">International transfers</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">If personal information is transferred outside the United Kingdom, we will take steps required by applicable data protection law to ensure that it receives an appropriate level of protection.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">How long we keep information</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy, including to provide services, maintain business records and meet legal, accounting or reporting requirements. The appropriate retention period depends on the type of information and why it was collected.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Cookies and website analytics</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Our website may use cookies or similar technologies to make the site work, remember preferences and understand how visitors use it. Where required, we will ask for your consent before using non-essential cookies. You can manage cookies through your browser settings and, where available, our website’s cookie controls. Disabling cookies may affect some website features.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Keeping information secure</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorised access, loss, misuse or disclosure. No method of transmitting or storing information is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Your rights</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to request access to your personal information, have it corrected or erased, restrict or object to its processing, receive certain information in a portable format, or withdraw consent. These rights are subject to legal conditions and exemptions. To exercise a right, contact us using the contact details provided on our website.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">You also have the right to complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO). Information about making a complaint is available at ico.org.uk. We would appreciate the opportunity to address your concerns first.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Children</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Our services and website are not intended to be directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through them.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Links to other websites</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Our website may contain links to third-party websites. We are not responsible for their privacy practices. Please review the privacy information on any external website you visit.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Changes to this policy</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">We may update this policy from time to time. The latest version will be published on our website with its updated date.</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">Contact us</p>
                                        <p class="MarginTopEightElement">For questions about this policy or how we handle personal information, contact Stone and Story using the contact details provided on our website.</p>
